d><oa:hasTarget rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/1200/044_Id_19"/><oa:hasBody rdf:resource="http://www.europeana.eu/schemas/epf/metadataTierC"/></dqv:QualityAnnotation></dqv:hasQualityAnnotation></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/1200/044_Id_19"><dc:creator>Salvator Rosa</dc:creator><dc:creator rdf:resource="http://viaf.org/viaf/97748522"></dc:creator><dc:date>ca. 1647</dc:date><dc:description xml:lang="en">As well as demonstrating the painter's erudition, the use of Greek may also have served a symbolic purpose. In this painting, the artist is shown inscribing a skull with a Greek text that may read: "Behold: whither, sometime". The artist uses the language of timeless wisdom to write on an object symbolising the transience of human existence. This juxtaposition heightens the contrast between the eternal and the transient, which is the message of the painted scene.</dc:description><dc:format xml:lang="en">Painting</dc:format><dc:identifier>Inv. 21.105</dc:identifier><dc:language>Greek</dc:language><dc:subject rdf:resource="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q359421"></dc:subject><dc:subject rdf:resource="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q808561"></dc:subject><dc:subject xml:lang="en">Salvator Rosa</dc:subject><dc:subject xml:lang="en">Baroque painting</dc:subject><dc:title xml:lang="en">Self-portrait</dc:title><dcterms:isPartOf xml:lang="en">GrECI</dcterms:isPartOf><dcterms:medium xml:lang="en">Oil on Canvas</dcterms:medium><dcterms:provenance xml:lang="en">New York, Metropolitan Museum of Art</dcterms:provenance><dcterms:spatial rdf:resource="https://sws.geonames.org/11874039/"></dcterms:spatial><dcterms:temporal rdf:resource="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7016"></dcterms:temporal><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/1200/044_Id_19"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/1200/044_Id_19"/><edm:type